; A segment's frames. Two cards a segment in (n, send); for each frame j out, five cards to the chooser (j, u, wl,
; wr, end) and u twice more, for the pitch and the level. u = (10 j + 5) / n, the frame's place in
; the segment in tenths, by taking n away. wl and wr weigh the glides at the segment's start and end: the first frame
; 3 and the second 9 when n is 4 or more, the first 3 when n is 3; when n is 2 only the start glides, wl 5 for the
; first frame, and the second frame keeps the segment's own target. end is 1 for the last frame of the pause that
; ends everything (send 3): send - k - 3 is 0 there and less everywhere else.
;
; Address Contents Label Opcode Operand Comment
  03            seg     INP   n        03-09: a segment; a pause can have no frames
  04                    INP   send
  05                    CLA   z
  06                    STO   j
  07                    CLA   n
  08                    SUB   00
  09                    TAC   seg
  10            frm     CLA   j        10-23: u
  11                    SFT   10
  12                    ADD   five
  13                    STO   r
  14                    CLA   z
  15                    STO   u
  16            ul1     CLA   r
  17                    SUB   n
  18                    TAC   wts
  19                    STO   r
  20                    CLA   u
  21                    ADD   00
  22                    STO   u
  23                    JMP   ul1
  24            wts     CLA   j        24-33: wl from j, wr from n - 1 - j
  25                    STO   k
  26                    JMP   wgt
  27                    STO   wl
  28                    CLA   n
  29                    SUB   00
  30                    SUB   j
  31                    STO   k
  32                    JMP   wgt
  33                    STO   wr
  34                    CLA   z        34-48: end, then the cards
  35                    STO   e
  36                    CLA   send
  37                    SUB   k
  38                    SUB   n3
  39                    TAC   outs
  40                    CLA   00
  41                    STO   e
  42            outs    OUT   j
  43                    OUT   u
  44                    OUT   wl
  45                    OUT   wr
  46                    OUT   e
  47            up      OUT   u
  48            ul      OUT   u
  49                    CLA   j        49-54: the next frame
  50                    ADD   00
  51                    STO   j
  52                    SUB   n
  53                    TAC   frm
  54                    JMP   seg
  55            wgt     CLA   99       55-96: the weight of the frame k from a segment's end
  56                    STO   ret
  57                    CLA   k
  58                    SUB   00
  59                    TAC   k0
  60                    SUB   00
  61                    TAC   k1
  62                    JMP   w0
  63            k1      CLA   n
  64                    SUB   n4
  65                    TAC   w0
  66                    CLA   c9
  67                    JMP   ret
  68            k0      CLA   n
  69                    SUB   n2
  70                    TAC   w0
  71                    SUB   00
  72                    TAC   w5
  73                    CLA   n3
  74                    JMP   ret
  75            w5b     CLA   five
  76                    JMP   ret
  77            w5      CLA   j        n is 2: 5 for the first frame (j 0), which only the start's glide asks for
  78                    SUB   00
  79                    TAC   w5b
  80            w0      CLA   z
  81            ret     DATA  0
  82            n       DATA  0
  83            send    DATA  0
  84            j       DATA  0
  85            u       DATA  0
  86            r       DATA  0
  87            k       DATA  0
  88            wl      DATA  0
  89            wr      DATA  0
  90            e       DATA  0
  91            z       DATA  0
  92            five    DATA  5
  93            n2      DATA  2
  94            n3      DATA  3
  95            n4      DATA  4
  96            c9      DATA  9
